    <section id="not-just-kids" class="audience-section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="section-kicker">Not all robot dogs are for kids</p>
        <h2>Some of the most interesting robot dogs are better gifts for adults — and some are built for seniors</h2>
        <p>
          The phrase “robot dog toy” hides two important audiences. Serious programmable quadrupeds can
          be excellent adult maker tools, while soft companion robot dogs serve a completely different
          need for older adults who value familiarity and simple interaction over coding.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="adult-grid">
        <article>
          <span class="audience-label">For adult makers</span>
          <h3>MechDog, Bittle and PuppyPi are robotics platforms first</h3>
          <p>
            If the recipient enjoys Python, Arduino, ROS, sensors, computer vision or mechanical motion,
            do not steer them toward a child-focused toy just because the search term says “robot dog”.
            MechDog is the accessible value entry, Bittle is the open-source maker pick, and PuppyPi is
            the high-end AI/ROS platform.
          </p>
          <div class="mini-links"><a href="#mechdog">MechDog</a><a href="#bittle">Bittle X V2</a><a href="#puppypi">PuppyPi</a></div>
        </article>

        <article id="chongker" class="companion-card">
          <span class="audience-label">For seniors / elderly companion use</span>
          <h3>Chongker Companion Robot Dog</h3>
          <p>
            This is deliberately not ranked against PuppyPi or Loona. The Chongker plush companion dog
            is designed around a familiar pet-like experience: soft body, voice interaction and heartbeat /
            purring-style feedback rather than coding, cameras or autonomous navigation.
          </p>
          <div class="fact-grid fact-grid--compact">
            <div><span>Observed price</span><strong>$99</strong><small>Border Collie / Golden Dog variants shown</small></div>
            <div><span>Amazon signal</span><strong>4.5★</strong><small>615 reviews shown on one listing</small></div>
            <div><span>Best for</span><strong>Low-complexity companionship</strong><small>not a developer robot</small></div>
          </div>
